{"data":{"body":"[P2] Apply the backend's status-disparity rules when selecting the chained parent. Hard-coding `()` means an X-Ray span normalized from canonical `UNSET` to `OK` cannot match a `status: UNSET` parent selector despite the backend declaring `UNSET_STATUS`, so a conformant trace fails before carrier and ancestry validation. Thread `feature_disparities` into this function and use the normal exact-first/fallback selector logic; add an X-Ray-style `UNSET`/`OK` regression test.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOTa1Cx88AAAABACtoQA","finding_digest":"5d54430357c68e748b106d1f5f67c09ee576c4eda0eae30c2f6488a96478eb52","finding_id":"arf_v1_lvkega2xy2hhjcyqnupv6z6at3","finding_key":"packages/aws-durable-execution-conformance-tests-otel/src/aws_durable_execution_conformance_tests_otel/validators.py::_chained_invoke_errors::backend-disparity-aware-parent-selection","identity_key":"packages/aws-durable-execution-conformance-tests-otel/src/aws_durable_execution_conformance_tests_otel/validators.py::_chained_invoke_errors::backend-disparity-aware-parent-selection","line":1273,"observation_digest":"381df75b85c54b2082b31503f4c971a9f8b698866236a766bd887a0856426218","observation_id":"aro_v1_hao7ow4fyvfsbavtcub7jslrvh","path":"packages/aws-durable-execution-conformance-tests-otel/src/aws_durable_execution_conformance_tests_otel/validators.py","prior_finding_id":"","published_at":"2026-10-16T18:07:30Z","review_id":"arr_v1_rd4444w3svluoon3jg4jcoijfr","reviewed_base_sha":"2387bb48968f7420ddf55aaf6dc83a9f15778332","reviewed_head_sha":"5a130a28713c21f78d7814713816b22138a0218f","reviewer":"codex","start_line":1273,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":131},"record_id":"art_v1_jm4bfn4fhat3qddr2nmhxuyfpu","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-10-16T18:07:30Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-conformance-tests","id":1303200455},"schema_version":1}
